#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Nepomuk Shell is a developer tool which allows to browse, query, and "
"edit Nepomuk resources. It is intended for debugging purposes only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The application has three basic modes: Resource browsing, SPARQL querying, "
"and Resource editing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <guilabel>Browse Resources</guilabel> mode a tree view shows all the "
"available classes/types that are stored in the Nepomuk database (by default "
"only the pimo:Thing subtree is shown. All resource types can be selected via "
"the combo box on top of the type tree). Clicking on a type will query all "
"resources of that type and display them in the left-hand view from where "
"they can be deleted or edited by double clicking on them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In SPARQL <guilabel>Query Resources</guilabel> mode one can enter a query in "
"the upper view. On clicking the <guibutton>Query</guibutton> button or using "
"the <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Enter;</keycombo> shortcut the query "
"is executed and the results are shown in the lower view. Again resource "
"nodes can be double clicked to edit them in editing mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All standard prefixes used in the Nepomuk ontologies are supported by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <guilabel>Edit Resource</guilabel> mode one sees two main views: the "
"properties/relations of the resource and the backlinks. The latter contain "
"all relations that contain the edited resource as an object. As before "
"resources can be double clicked to be edited. In addition literal values can "
"be edited in place. Be aware though that editing literal values in place "
"will not update their creation date. Here it becomes obvious that "
"<application>Nepomukshell</application> is not an end-user tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Above the relations view the statement creation widget allows to easily "
"create new relations by first inserting the property and in a second step "
"the object, &ie; a literal or a resource."
msgstr ""
